.TH XUR.STD.LOG 7 "2026-10-29" "xur 0.1.2" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.log \- structured logging
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::log;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::log
provides structured logging backed by the
.B tracing
ecosystem. A subscriber is configured with a builder, then log
functions emit events at different severity levels.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B subscriber() -> SubscriberBuilder
Create a new subscriber builder with default settings.
.TP
.B trace(format, args...)
Emit a trace-level event.
.TP
.B debug(format, args...)
Emit a debug-level event.
.TP
.B info(format, args...)
Emit an info-level event.
.TP
.B warn(format, args...)
Emit a warning-level event.
.TP
.B error(format, args...)
Emit an error-level event.
.SH SUBSCRIBERBUILDER METHODS
.TP
.B with_max_level(level) -> SubscriberBuilder
Set the maximum log level.
.I level
is
.BR \(dqtrace\(dq ,
.BR \(dqdebug\(dq ,
.BR \(dqinfo\(dq ,
.BR \(dqwarn\(dq ,
or
.BR \(dqerror\(dq .
.TP
.B with_target(bool) -> SubscriberBuilder
Show or hide the target (module path) in output.
.TP
.B with_file(bool) -> SubscriberBuilder
Show or hide the source file name.
.TP
.B with_line_number(bool) -> SubscriberBuilder
Show or hide the line number.
.TP
.B with_ansi(bool) -> SubscriberBuilder
Enable or disable ANSI colour codes.
.TP
.B json() -> SubscriberBuilder
Output events as JSON.
.TP
.B pretty() -> SubscriberBuilder
Use the pretty (multi-line) output format.
.TP
.B compact() -> SubscriberBuilder
Use the compact (single-line) output format.
.TP
.B with_filter(directive) -> SubscriberBuilder
Apply an
.B EnvFilter
directive, e.g.\&
.BR \(dqinfo,mymodule=debug\(dq .
.TP
.B to_file(path) -> SubscriberBuilder
Write log output to a file instead of stderr.
.TP
.B to_stderr() -> SubscriberBuilder
Write log output to stderr (the default).
.TP
.B init()
Install the subscriber as the global default. Call once at startup.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::log;
use std::io;

fn main() {
    log::subscriber()
        .with_max_level("debug")
        .with_ansi(true)
        .init();

    log::info("application started");
    log::debug("value: {}", 42);
    log::warn("something to watch");
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.io (7)
